  "scope": "Complete unmodified PlayerSaver.kt and PlayerSaveParser.kt, including populate/save/parse/parseData/runContentHooks and real save-file I/O in owned temporary directories with file.encoding=UTF-8. Also complete unmodified VarpManager, JSONUtils, PersistPlayer, GraveType, GameAttributes, SavedData/ActivityData/QuestData/GlobalData, IronmanManager/IronmanMode, SpellBookManager, BodyPart, Gender, MusicEntry and PetDetails, and the complete original timer and Item/Container classes of the timers and inventory oracles. Verbatim selected members only for Skills, Settings, Appearance, BankPinManager, EmoteManager, Properties, Entity, Player, Bank/EquipmentContainer, Location and ServerConstants. Recording adapters for quests, house, familiars/pets, music player, achievement diaries, pouches, POH storage, graves, autocast spells and content hooks; they hold getter values and record parser hand-offs, and do not model those systems. kotlinx.coroutines is a same-thread oracle stand-in. ServerConstants.JAVA_VERSION is fixed at 11; the script-engine pretty-printing branch, default-charset behaviour, a null save path, world login/logout wiring and concurrent saving are outside this corpus. Appended state cases: a second compilation of the unmodified PlayerSaver.kt and PlayerSaveParser.kt over the complete unmodified QuestRepository, Quest, Quests, MusicPlayer, MusicEntry, EmoteManager, AchievementDiaryManager, AchievementDiary, DiaryType, DiaryLevel, Bar, PouchManager, StorageState, StorageContainer, StorableFamily, SpellBookManager, Plugin, PluginManifest, PluginType and CloseEvent. Verbatim selected members: GraveController (ATTR_GTYPE, getGraveType, updateGraveType), ContentAPI (setAttribute, getAttribute, setVarp), Entity (setAttribute, getAttribute, removeAttribute), HouseManager (location, style, crest, rooms and servant fields with their getters and setters) and EquipmentContainer slot constants. Emotes, HouseLocation, HousingStyle and CrestType are generated with the original constant names and order only; org.rs09.consts.Items constants take the number that ends their name. Familiars, pets, house loading and content hooks stay recording adapters. Packet dispatch, interface manager, packets, GameWorld, NPCDefinition, events, the remaining ContentAPI functions and Skills.getLevel are stand-ins outside the driven paths; container listeners record. Quest registration, songs, spells and item definitions are scripted oracle inputs, not the pinned content.",
  "sourceHashAlgorithm": "sha256, CR removed",
